    bodyContent: `<h2>What We're Actually Comparing Here</h2><p>These two tools aren't really competitors. Housecall Pro is a field service management (FSM) platform. AutoGrowth AI is a revenue recovery system. I'll be honest — a lot of contractors run both at the same time, and it makes sense once you understand what each one actually does.</p><p>Here's the thing: Housecall Pro won't answer your phone at 11pm when a homeowner's AC dies. It won't chase down the estimate you sent last Tuesday. And it's not going to bug your happy customers until they leave you a Google review. That's not what it's built for. AutoGrowth AI is built for exactly that.</p><h2>Feature Comparison</h2><table><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Housecall Pro</th><th>AutoGrowth AI</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Scheduling & Dispatch</td><td>✅ Yes</td><td>❌ Not built for this</td></tr><tr><td>Invoicing & Payments</td><td>✅ Yes</td><td>❌ Not built for this</td></tr><tr><td>Online Booking</td><td>✅ Yes</td><td>❌ Not built for this</td></tr><tr><td>QuickBooks Integration</td><td>✅ Yes</td><td>❌ Not built for this</td></tr><tr><td>24/7 AI Phone Answering</td><td>❌ No</td><td>✅ Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Missed Call Recovery</td><td>❌ No</td><td>✅ Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Estimate Follow-Up Sequences</td><td>❌ No</td><td>✅ Yes</td></tr><tr><td>Review Generation Automation</td><td>❌ No</td><td>✅ Yes</td></tr><tr><td>CSR / Marketing AI</td><td>✅ Add-on</td><td>✅ Core feature</td></tr><tr><td>HVAC-Specific Integration (Bluon)</td><td>✅ Yes</td><td>❌ No</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Look, Housecall Pro covers your operations. AutoGrowth AI covers your revenue leaks. Two different problems, two different tools.</p><h2>Pricing Comparison</h2><h3>Housecall Pro</h3><ul><li><strong>Basic:</strong> $59/month — 1 user, core scheduling and invoicing</li><li><strong>Plus:</strong> $149/month — up to 5 users, online booking, QuickBooks sync</li><li><strong>Pro:</strong> $299/month — up to 20 users, advanced reporting, priority support</li></ul><p>Their CSR AI and Marketing AI tools are available as add-ons at additional cost. If you want Bluon integration for HVAC parts pricing, that's built in at the higher tiers.</p><h3>AutoGrowth AI</h3><p>AutoGrowth AI pricing is based on your business size and what you need covered. Request a free audit at <a href="/audit">/audit</a> and you'll get actual numbers, not a sales runaround. Most HVAC contractors see the cost offset fast when they stop losing $300-$800 jobs to missed calls.</p><h2>Pros and Cons</h2><h3>Housecall Pro</h3><ul><li><strong>Pro:</strong> Best-in-class scheduling and dispatch for 1-20 tech teams</li><li><strong>Pro:</strong> Clean invoicing, solid payment processing</li><li><strong>Pro:</strong> QuickBooks integration actually works (I know that sounds basic, but it matters)</li><li><strong>Pro:</strong> Bluon integration is a genuine win for HVAC shops tracking parts</li><li><strong>Pro:</strong> Good mobile app for techs in the field</li><li><strong>Con:</strong> Won't recover missed calls or follow up on dead estimates</li><li><strong>Con:</strong> Review generation is not automated — it's manual at best</li><li><strong>Con:</strong> CSR AI and Marketing AI cost extra and aren't as focused on revenue recovery</li><li><strong>Con:</strong> If you grow past 20 techs, pricing jumps fast</li></ul><h3>AutoGrowth AI</h3><ul><li><strong>Pro:</strong> 24/7 AI answering means you stop losing jobs when your office is closed</li><li><strong>Pro:</strong> Missed call recovery texts leads back within minutes — not hours</li><li><strong>Pro:</strong> Estimate follow-up sequences close more jobs without anyone doing it manually</li><li><strong>Pro:</strong> Review generation runs on autopilot — your Google rating actually goes up</li><li><strong>Pro:</strong> Works alongside whatever FSM you're already using</li><li><strong>Con:</strong> Not a replacement for scheduling or invoicing software — you still need that</li><li><strong>Con:</strong> If you have zero leads coming in, lead gen comes first before this helps</li></ul><h2>Best For</h2><h3>Choose Housecall Pro if:</h3><p>You need to get your operations organized. If techs are running on paper or spreadsheets, start with Housecall Pro. It's well-built for teams of 1-20 and the pricing is fair for what you get. I'd go Plus at minimum — Basic is pretty bare.</p><h3>Choose AutoGrowth AI if:</h3><p>You've already got an FSM or you're handling scheduling fine, but you're bleeding money somewhere else. Missed calls after hours. Estimates you sent that just died. Happy customers who never leave reviews. That's the stuff AutoGrowth AI fixes.</p><h3>Run Both if:</h3><p>Honestly? Most established HVAC shops should be running both. Housecall Pro handles your ops. AutoGrowth AI handles the revenue you're currently leaving on the table. They don't step on each other. A lot of contractors who use Housecall Pro add AutoGrowth AI specifically because the FSM doesn't touch any of the after-hours or follow-up problems.</p><h2>Bottom Line</h2><p>Don't pit these against each other like you have to pick one. If your operations are a mess, fix that first — Housecall Pro is a good call. If your ops are dialed in but you're still losing jobs to missed calls and ghosted estimates, AutoGrowth AI is the fix. And if you want to stop losing money on both fronts, run them together.</p><p>I've talked to contractors running $2M shops who still miss 20-30% of their inbound calls after hours. That's real money walking out the door every week. AutoGrowth AI is specifically built to stop that.</p><h2>See How AutoGrowth AI Works For Your Business — Free Audit</h2><p>No pitch deck. No demo where someone reads slides at you. Just a real look at where your shop is losing revenue and what it would take to fix it.</p><p><a href="/audit"><strong>Get Your Free Audit → /audit</strong></a></p>`,
