    blufBlock: `**Jobber is one of the best field service management tools out there for small HVAC and home service shops — buy it if you need scheduling, invoicing, and dispatch.** **But if you're losing jobs to voicemail and letting leads go cold, AutoGrowth AI plugs the holes Jobber doesn't touch.**`,
    bodyContent: `<h2>What You're Actually Comparing Here</h2><p>These two aren't really fighting each other. Jobber runs your operations. AutoGrowth AI runs your lead capture and follow-up. I run both. Most serious contractors should think about both.</p><p>But if you're trying to decide where to spend money first, or you're wondering what each one actually does — here's the breakdown.</p><h2>Feature Comparison</h2><table style='width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;'><thead><tr><th style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;text-align:left;'>Feature</th><th style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;text-align:left;'>Jobber</th><th style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;text-align:left;'>AutoGrowth AI</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>Scheduling & Dispatch</td><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>✅ Strong</td><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>❌ Not its job</td></tr><tr><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>Route Optimization</td><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>✅ Yes</td><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>❌ No</td></tr><tr><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>Online Booking</td><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>✅ Yes</td><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>❌ No</td></tr><tr><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>Invoicing & Quotes</td><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>✅ Yes</td><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>❌ No</td></tr><tr><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>QuickBooks Integration</td><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>✅ Yes</td><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>❌ No</td></tr><tr><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>Recurring Jobs</td><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>✅ Yes</td><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>❌ No</td></tr><tr><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>Customer Portal</td><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>✅ Yes</td><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>❌ No</td></tr><tr><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>AI Phone Answering</td><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>❌ No</td><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>✅ Yes</td></tr><tr><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>Missed Call Text-Back</td><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>❌ No</td><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>✅ Yes</td></tr><tr><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>Lead Follow-Up Automation</td><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>❌ No</td><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>✅ Yes</td></tr><tr><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>Review Campaign Automation</td><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>❌ No</td><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>✅ Yes</td></tr><tr><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>AI Scheduling Assistant</td><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>✅ Yes (Connect+)</td><td style='border:1px solid #ccc;padding:8px;'>❌ No</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Look, the table tells the story. Jobber owns the operations side. AutoGrowth AI owns the front-end lead stuff — answering calls, texting back missed calls, chasing leads that went quiet, and getting you more reviews on autopilot.</p><h2>Pricing Comparison</h2><h3>Jobber</h3><ul><li><strong>Core: $39/month</strong> — 1 user, basic scheduling and invoicing. Fine for solo operators.</li><li><strong>Connect: $129/month</strong> — Up to 5 users. Adds online booking, QuickBooks sync, two-way texting, and the AI scheduling assistant.</li><li><strong>Grow: $249/month</strong> — Up to 15 users. Adds quote follow-ups, referral tracking, and more reporting.</li></ul><p>Here's the thing — most shops I talk to are on Connect at $129. That's the sweet spot for a crew of 2-5 guys. It's a fair price for what you get.</p><h3>AutoGrowth AI</h3><p>AutoGrowth AI pricing is based on your business size and which features you turn on. The core pitch is simple: if it books even one extra job a week that you would've lost to voicemail, it pays for itself fast. Get the actual numbers at the <a href='/audit'>free audit</a>.</p><h2>Pros and Cons</h2><h3>Jobber — Pros</h3><ul><li>Genuinely great scheduling and dispatch. One of the best in the market for small shops.</li><li>Route optimization actually saves your techs time on the road.</li><li>Online booking is clean and customers can use it without calling you.</li><li>QuickBooks integration works without a headache.</li><li>Mobile app is solid. Techs can use it in the field without complaining.</li><li>Built for 1-20 employees — it doesn't try to be everything for everyone.</li></ul><h3>Jobber — Cons</h3><ul><li>Won't answer your phone when you're under a crawlspace.</li><li>No missed call text-back. Customer calls, goes to voicemail, calls your competitor.</li><li>Lead follow-up is manual. If you forget, the lead dies.</li><li>No automated review campaigns. You have to ask customers yourself, which most contractors never do consistently.</li><li>Price jumps hard from Core to Connect — $39 to $129 is a big step for a solo guy.</li></ul><h3>AutoGrowth AI — Pros</h3><ul><li>Answers every call, even at 11pm on a Saturday.</li><li>Missed call text-back fires immediately. Customer knows you saw their call.</li><li>Lead follow-up runs on its own. You don't have to remember to chase anyone.</li><li>Review campaigns run automatically after jobs close. Your Google rating goes up without you doing anything.</li><li>Pays for itself with one or two recovered jobs a month.</li></ul><h3>AutoGrowth AI — Cons</h3><ul><li>I'll be honest — it doesn't do scheduling, invoicing, or any of the ops stuff. You still need a tool like Jobber for that.</li><li>It's a lead and reputation tool, not a business management platform.</li><li>If your main problem is disorganized scheduling — start with Jobber first.</li></ul><h2>Best For</h2><h3>Buy Jobber If:</h3><ul><li>You have 1-20 employees and need real scheduling and dispatch software.</li><li>Your techs need a mobile app they can use on the job.</li><li>You're invoicing out of spreadsheets or your head and it's becoming a problem.</li><li>You want QuickBooks to stop being a nightmare.</li></ul><h3>Use AutoGrowth AI If:</h3><ul><li>You're missing calls and losing jobs to voicemail.</li><li>Your leads go cold because nobody follows up fast enough.</li><li>You have under 50 Google reviews and your competitor has 200.</li><li>You want your phone to work for you while you're actually working.</li></ul><h3>Use Both If:</h3><ul><li>You're running a real operation and you want Jobber handling the back end while AutoGrowth AI captures every lead on the front end. That's the setup that actually makes sense for a growing shop.</li></ul><h2>Bottom Line</h2><p>Jobber is legitimately good software. I'm not here to talk you out of it. If you need field service management, it belongs in your stack.</p><p>But Jobber doesn't answer your phone. It doesn't text back missed calls. It doesn't chase leads or run review campaigns. That's money walking out the door every week — and that's exactly what AutoGrowth AI is built to stop.</p><p>Most contractors need both. Start with whichever gap is costing you more money right now.</p><p style='margin-top:32px;'><a href='/audit' style='background:#f97316;color:#fff;padding:14px 28px;border-radius:6px;text-decoration:none;font-weight:bold;font-size:1rem;'>See How AutoGrowth AI Works For Your Business — Free Audit</a></p>`,
